# TEMPLATE -- NOT APPLIED (the `.example` suffix keeps kustomize from picking it
# up, and no plaintext secret is ever committed; see PLAN.md "No plaintext
# secrets").
#
# How to produce the real file:
#
#   1. Create a FINE-GRAINED GitHub personal access token, scoped to the single
#      repository `<github-org>/homelab-infrastructure`, with exactly:
#         Repository permissions -> Contents:      Read and write
#         Repository permissions -> Pull requests: Read and write
#      Nothing else. No org permissions, no `workflow` scope (Renovate only edits
#      workflow files if you grant it, and a classic PAT with `workflow` would be
#      a far bigger blast radius). Set a 90-day expiry and rotate.
#
#   2. Fill the values below, then encrypt IN PLACE with the repo-wide mechanism
#      chosen by topic 3 (actions-runner-controller):
#
#        SOPS:            cp secret.sops.yaml.example secret.sops.yaml
#                         sops --encrypt --in-place secret.sops.yaml
#                         (add `- secret.sops.yaml` to kustomization.yaml and make
#                          sure Kustomization/infra-controllers in
#                          clusters/homelab/infrastructure.yaml has
#                          decryption.secretRef -> sops-age)
#
#        SealedSecrets:   kubeseal --format yaml < secret.sops.yaml.example \
#                           > sealedsecret.yaml
#                         (commit sealedsecret.yaml instead and reference it)
#
#   3. `GITHUB_COM_TOKEN` is optional: a read-only, no-scope classic token used
#      solely to fetch changelogs/release notes from public repos without hitting
#      the anonymous GitHub API rate limit. Omit the key and the CronJob still
#      works (it is referenced with `optional: true`).
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: renovate-token
  namespace: renovate
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: renovate
    app.kubernetes.io/part-of: homelab
type: Opaque
stringData:
  RENOVATE_TOKEN: github_pat_REPLACE_ME
  GITHUB_COM_TOKEN: ghp_REPLACE_ME_OR_DELETE_THIS_KEY
